@startuml isolation-tenancy
' ============================================================================
' agentd platform — ISOLATION model (2026-07-18). How one user's agent NEVER
' touches another's, and why the guarantee is the KERNEL/MOUNT boundary, not a
' path-string check. Two blocks: (1) tenancy walls, (2) cross-turn continuity.
' PUML only; do not render PNG unless asked.
' ============================================================================
title Isolation — two users on one fleet, four independent walls

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 17
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #888888
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C8B900
}

actor "User A" as A
actor "User B" as B

package "COMPUTE (shared, holds no data)" as CMP #EAF3FF {
  rectangle "Hosted Runtime engine fleet\nONE service serves everyone;\neach CONNECTION resolves its own\nuser_id from the verified token" as FLEET
  rectangle "Sandbox for A's run\nmounts ONLY /users/A/agents/*\nzero-perm role - no internal VPC" as SBXA #FFF0F0
}

package "STATE plane (durable, per-user)" as ST #FFF0F0 {
  database "/users/A/\nagents - sessions - memory" as RA
  database "/users/B/\nagents - sessions - memory" as RB
}

A --> FLEET : conn A (token -> user_id=A)
B --> FLEET : conn B (token -> user_id=B)
FLEET --> RA : A's turn: rooted at /users/A only
FLEET --> RB : B's turn: rooted at /users/B only
FLEET --> SBXA : dispatch A's custom/exec tool
SBXA --> RA : mount ONLY A's agent dir\n(EFS Access Point)
SBXA ..> RB : B NOT mounted -> does not exist to it

note bottom of CMP
  WALL 1 IDENTITY: user_id comes from the verified account token, never the client.
  WALL 2 PATHS (defense-in-depth): the shared engine roots every read at /users/<uid>/
     AND never exposes exec / custom-plugin tools (a path check alone can't contain a shell).
  WALL 3 KERNEL/MOUNT (the guarantee): arbitrary code runs ONLY in a sandbox that
     mounts just that user's dir — a neighbour's path is physically absent, not merely blocked.
  WALL 4 IDENTITY/NET (IAM): the sandbox role reaches only that user's storage; no provider
     keys, no DB creds, no internal VPC.
end note
@enduml


@startuml cross-turn-continuity
title Cross-turn continuity — results persist because STATE does, not the process

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 16
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor #888888
  ParticipantBackgroundColor White
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C8B900
}

participant "Agent loop\n(engine)" as L
participant "Sandbox\n(ephemeral)" as S
database "User's durable state\n/users/uid (EFS/S3)" as D
participant "Session transcript\n(also durable)" as T

== Turn 1 — produce a result ==
L -> S : dispatch tool (mounts /users/uid/agents/id)
S -> D : write output to workspace/ (durable)
S -> S : scratch in VM /tmp (will vanish)
S --> L : ToolResult + artifact REFERENCE (a path/id)
L -> T : record the reference in history
note right of S : sandbox DIES — its scratch is gone,\nbut the workspace file remains in D

== Turn 5 — refer back, later ==
L -> T : load history (still has the reference)
L -> S : dispatch a FRESH sandbox\n(mounts the SAME /users/uid/agents/id)
S -> D : read the earlier artifact back
S --> L : uses it — seamless

note over L, D
  Continuity = durable per-user STATE, not a long-lived process. Nothing stays
  running between turns; the next sandbox re-reads the same folder. Discipline:
  tools write durable outputs to the mounted workspace, never to VM-local /tmp.
end note
@enduml
